      "sourceTextSha256": "dc4c0196ca3c690c27beb4865794aa34dcc587e9cfea33c38334b376995bac3c",
      "text": "Day 2 · Corcovado and Christ the Redeemer (6 hours, lunch included). After breakfast, meet your guide in the lobby. An eco-friendly train climbs through the Tijuca Forest, home to monkeys and exotic birds, to the summit of Corcovado where, at 710 metres, stands the symbol of Rio, the 38-metre statue of Christ the Redeemer, built in 1931, with a breathtaking panorama of the Rio–Niterói Bridge, Guanabara Bay, the Botanical Garden, the legendary Maracanã Stadium and Sugar Loaf. Lunch in a typical Brazilian restaurant.",
